    "Question_Text": "According to the passage, ecological gene drives targeting disease vectors carry systemic risks because:",
    "Option_A": "Eradicating insect populations can precipitate unpredictable non-linear trophic cascades and ecosystem destabilization.",
    "Option_B": "It proves that bacteria can be eradicated completely using chemical antibiotics.",
    "Option_C": "It demonstrates that genetic modifications are naturally rejected by cellular repair mechanisms.",
    "Option_D": "It shows that DNA sequencing has become completely cost-free and ubiquitous.",
    "Correct_Answer": "A",
    "Marks": 1,
    "Difficulty_Level": "MEDIUM",
    "Explanation": "Authoritative analysis of Set C Passage 1, Question 7: The passage addresses CRISPR mechanics, gene drives, bioethics, and regulatory divergence.",
